<title>SINGAPORE: Nobel gets nod for listing on Singapore's SESDAQ.</title>
<headline>Nobel gets nod for listing on Singapore's SESDAQ.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-10-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Interior design and furniture company Nobel group Holdings Ltd said on Wednesday it had received in-principle approval from the Stock Exchange of Singapore (SES) to list on the island's secondary board SESDAQ.</p>
<p>A Nobel statement gave no details of its initial public offering (IPO) of shares but the SES usually requires companies to launch their share offers within a couple of months of receiving approval.</p>
<p>Nobel said it had a turnover of Singapore $29.6 million in the year ended December 31, 1996.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703199)</p>
